# /etc/sudoers.d/openmarquee — passwordless sudo for the openmarquee user.
#
# Installed to /etc/sudoers.d/openmarquee (mode 0440) two ways, both
# `visudo -c`-validated so a malformed file can never brick a device:
#   1. baked into the SD image at build time by the stage-openmarquee
#      04-ssh-user substage (files/ overlay + a visudo -c gate), so the
#      grant is present on a fresh card independent of cloud-init;
#   2. re-applied by scripts/install.sh on every (re)deploy.
#
# Scope: FULL passwordless sudo (qarl's explicit call 2026-07-13). The
# `openmarquee` user now does double duty — it is BOTH the systemd service
# user (openmarquee-backend et al., User=openmarquee) AND the key-only SSH
# login identity on shipped devices. Operational work over that SSH login
# (systemctl, deploy, backup, install/admin) needs broad sudo, so this is
# deliberately NOT scoped down.
#
# SECURITY POSTURE (documented decision, not an oversight): because the
# login user, the service user, and full root-via-sudo are now the same
# identity, a compromise of the backend service reaches full root. Accepted
# per qarl's "we need install/admin" call. Scoping sudo to specific commands
# is possible future work once the operational surface is understood — not now.
#
# NOTE on reachability: openmarquee-backend.service sets NoNewPrivileges=true,
# which BLOCKS sudo from ITS context ("sudo: The 'no new privileges' flag is
# set") — its privileged network ops go through the socket-activated root
# daemon (openmarquee-netctl.socket) instead, no sudo needed. But NOT every
# service run as openmarquee sets NNP — e.g. openmarquee-tailscale.service does
# not — so this grant IS reachable from those service contexts too, which is
# exactly the blast radius the security-posture note above accepts. The grant's
# primary intended use is the interactive SSH login shell.
#
# WARNING: do not edit this file in place on a deployed Pi — install.sh
# overwrites it on every deploy. Make changes in the repo + redeploy.

openmarquee ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD:ALL
